{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(triangle_centers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (triangle centers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in an equilateral triangle, and a square is inscribed in the circle. \nThe ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the square is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffacb19b41ddce8d1be897024d8db289aad7f2d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{3}:1\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{3}:\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\sqrt{3}:2\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3:\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3:2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"580\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a745d91ec710600fe08581453dcc75c5a0428394.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),100)); draw((173.205,-100)--(-173.205,-100)--(0,200)--(173.205,-100)); draw((-100,0)--(0,100)--(100,0)--(0,-100)--(-100,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,-100),dotted); draw((0,0)--(-173.205,-100),dotted); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\nLet the radius of the circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  That means the diameter of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5745df50c8607bdc9b8de4968315633a3047dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, so the side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7b330b6f2f299d2fa2b76355d7a4942243a4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore, the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdc3bd06d3f13fde4505d5bf487f683e24ad96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>By using 30-60-90 triangles, half of the side length of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfca334c3f61ae13cdcb7160ac48e7916ca895f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so each side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9745a72c6d8b5390a846d06e27e6cb989787e7a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> units long.  Thus, the area of the equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/1405349a9234ecb18f2213d4a708fac70a7a9ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3r^2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The ratio of the area of the equilateral triangle to the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db93ab9ffbea8aeac1e7f7c3afbbfb51ccea375a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3r^2 \\sqrt{3}}{2r^2} = \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"41\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28triangle_centers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(triangle_centers)\">Solution 2 (triangle centers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (triangle centers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Refer to the diagram shown in Solution 1. Notice the dotted line that stretches to the bottom of the square/circle. This is the inradius of the equilateral triangle. If we know this length, we could find the side length of the square, and use the equilateral triangle area formula to find the ratio.\n</p><p>The inradius of any given triangle is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329ea72ead78b52d166d459894c44dc2370aa4aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\text{Area}}{\\text{semiperimeter}}.\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>We could specify this formula for an equilateral triangle (or if you memorized it for some reason):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f2496ea910b2217741165479fa7548a549a584.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s^{2}}{4}}{\\frac{3s}{2}} = \\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{6}.\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Denote this value as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Thus the area of the square is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d7a56b7a061a67bf8b485dc7e156feecb0fc17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r^{2} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{3s^{2}}{36} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{s^{2}}{12} = \\frac{s^{2}}{6}.\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Now ratio this to the area of the equilateral triangle,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997f35eadf0ca23cf9965fcf9eaf8d5c21e8b50a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s^{2}}{4}}{\\frac{s^{2}}{6}} = 6 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e480aa134bc797cdde761c7ac6b56638cbc21587.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</